From ea1b7aba3212ff4ab662827649a8439a575f9c1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 07:35:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add log tail modal to Logs page with configurable line count

Wires the Logs page's "More" button to a shared modal showing the last
N lines of a log's live (un-rotated) file, fetched fresh from a new
/logs/<filename>/tail JSON endpoint on each open rather than baking
content into the page at load time, since log files are large and
change constantly. Tail reading walks the file backwards in 8KB chunks
so it never loads the whole file into memory. The line count defaults
to 50 and is configurable in Settings > Logging (log_tail_lines),
capped at 2000 regardless of the configured value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GdhKf193j6ggwAGFYCUaJg
